# What a `zerg` walk does not enter in this repository.
#
# This file REPLACES `.gitignore` for `zerg fmt`, `zerg lint` and `zerg desugar` — one source
# of truth at a time, because two that both apply need an ordering between them and an ordering
# is what makes an ignore file unreadable. What `.gitignore` excludes and this does not —
# `/bin/`, `/.zerg-cache/`, `/dist/` — holds no `.zg` at all, so nothing is lost by the swap.

# THE CORPUS IS DELIBERATELY NOT CANONICAL. `test-data/` holds 488 sources, and the fmt corpus's
# inputs are non-canonical ON PURPOSE: that is what the gate compares against. Formatting them
# would not merely rewrite somebody's fixtures, it would leave `fmt-corpus` passing forever while
# measuring nothing.
#
# `.gitignore` cannot protect it — `git check-ignore test-data` answers nothing, because it is a
# tracked submodule rather than an ignored path.
test-data/
